            "confidence": "high",
            "summary": "This is a coherent document-to-poster tool, but its installer and HTML rendering pipeline create security risks that users should review before installing.",
            "dimensions": [
              {
                "detail": "Large ML/OCR dependencies, Chromium, outbound LLM/image API calls, and configurable API endpoints are mostly purpose-aligned, but the combination handles user documents and credentials with limited containment guidance.",
                "label": "Credentials",
                "name": "environment_proportionality",
                "rating": "concern"
              },
              {
                "detail": "Installation is disclosed, but install.sh and SKILL.md use an unverified remote curl-to-shell UV installer, install system packages with apt-get, install Playwright Chromium, and requirements.txt includes an unpinned Git dependency.",
                "label": "Install Mechanism",
                "name": "install_mechanism",
                "rating": "concern"
              },
              {
                "detail": "The skill asks the model to generate full HTML from user documents and then writes that HTML directly; conversion can load the result in a JavaScript-enabled Chromium context, so document-influenced model output may execute active browser content during PDF/PNG generation.",
                "label": "Instruction Scope",
                "name": "instruction_scope",
                "rating": "concern"
              },
              {
                "detail": "The artifacts create a virtual environment, install user/system dependencies, install Chromium, and create a .env template; I did not find background services, scheduled tasks, backdoors, or unrelated persistence.",
                "label": "Persistence & Privilege",
